      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on a 2022 F-150 with a slipping issue. my scan tool is showing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. what are the most likely things causing pressure fluctuations like that in an automatic transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Several issues could cause irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of an F-150. It might be a faulty transmission pressure sensor, leaks in the hydraulic fluid, or problems with the transmission control module (TCM). You should inspect the hydraulic lines for leaks, check the transmission fluid level, and it might be wise to have the transmission pressure sensor tested or replaced if necessary. If these steps don't solve the issue, it's recommended to consult with a professional technician for further diagnosis.",
